<!--
  The agent feature, M8. Every id and every word here is verbatim from
  docs/M8-copy.md, which the design seat owns; nothing in this file was
  written by engineering, and M8CopyTest proves that by reading both files
  rather than by anyone rereading them.

  Its own file for the same reason strings_m3_locked.xml is: strings.xml
  belongs to the M2 session and no seat edits another's file.

  Two things that look like omissions and are not:

  1. m3_locked_queued_transcript_label, m3_locked_queued_title,
     m3_locked_unlock_action and m3_locked_discard_action are reused verbatim
     from M3 and are deliberately not redefined. Two definitions of one id is
     a build failure, and the first one is not this seat's to move.
  2. m8_ambiguous_title is a plurals resource with an explicit "two" case,
     because "Two projects match" reads as prose at that length while "2"
     reads as a count in a report. Android has no "two" quantity for English,
     so the "two" case is carried as its own string and chosen in code; the
     plurals resource keeps the "other" form. Both are checked against the
     copy.

  The whole of section 2 is enforced elsewhere and not here: agent output is
  read, never spoken. Nothing in the spoken block below has a %s in it. The
  only substitutions any spoken string takes are project numbers.
-->
