    <!-- ==================================== answering a question
         Section 5.18, rewritten on 2026-09-21 against a question.asked captured on the
         wire. A question is not free text: a request carries a list of questions, each
         with labelled options, and two flags. multiple says whether more than one
         option may be chosen, custom whether an answer in the user's own words is
         accepted at all. So the options are the control, and dictation is the second
         way in, present only when custom is true. m8_run_answer_not_now and
         m8_run_answer_not_now_cd were retired in the same pass: closing the microphone
         exits nothing once the rows are on the screen.

         IT ASKED marks the question in the reply flow, in body, with section 1.2's two
         type treatments unchanged, and it marks a permission request in the same place
         for the same reason. The header field is not rendered at all. The question, the
         option labels and the option descriptions are all agent output: read, never
         heard, never announced, never put in the status label, which is the live
         region. The two announce strings say a question arrived and where the controls
         are, and differ only in whether they mention the microphone.

         CHOOSE ONE sends on the tap. CHOOSE ANY makes the rows checkable and adds Send,
         because with more than one allowed no tap can be read as the last one.
         Recommended is Maia's own chip: the agent appends "(Recommended)" to its label
         and Maia strips exactly that and nothing else. Question %1$d of %2$d shows only
         when the request carries more than one, and both numbers are counts of an
         array.

         YOUR ANSWER holds the live partial in 4b's treatment. An utterance that is
         exactly an option label selects that option; anything else goes as free text.
         The answer goes on the tap or when the user stops speaking, and nothing confirms
         first (5.10's rule); YOU ANSWERED with the answers under it is the receipt.

         Three ways out, two of which leave the turn running: Decide without me sends an
         empty answer list, Drop the question rejects it, and Stop interrupts the turn
         (m8_run_stop_action, reused). Neither marker takes a hairline, because neither
         ends the reply. On a failure what the user chose stays on screen: Send it again
         for a tunnel that came back, Say it again for a recogniser that got it wrong.
         IT DID NOT TAKE THAT is not IT STOPPED WAITING: an expired question and an
         answer that lost its way are the same answer on the wire, so the marker reports
         the transaction rather than the agent. -->
    <string name="m8_run_question_label">IT ASKED</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_announce">%1$d asked you something. What it asked is above, and the answers to choose from are at the bottom of the screen.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_announce_open">%1$d asked you something. What it asked is above, the answers to choose from are at the bottom of the screen, and the microphone is open.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_step">Question %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="m8_run_options_label">CHOOSE ONE</string>
    <string name="m8_run_options_label_many">CHOOSE ANY</string>
    <string name="m8_run_options_send">Send</string>
    <string name="m8_run_options_send_cd">Send. What you have ticked goes to the agent as your answer.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_option_recommended">Recommended</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_label">YOUR ANSWER</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_listening">The microphone is open. Say one of the answers, or say your own.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answered_question">YOU ANSWERED</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_skip">Decide without me</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_skip_cd">Decide without me. No answer goes, the agent is told you did not answer, and it carries on and decides for itself. Any questions after this one are left unanswered too.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_dismiss">Drop the question</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_dismiss_cd">Drop the question. It goes off the screen, the agent is told you turned it down, and the run carries on.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_skipped">YOU LET IT DECIDE</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_dismissed">YOU DROPPED THIS</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_nothing_heard">Nothing heard. The agent is still waiting, and the answers are still there.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_send_again">Send it again</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_send_again_cd">Send it again. The same answer goes, and the microphone does not open.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_say_again">Say it again</string>
    <string name="m8_run_answer_say_again_cd">Say it again. The microphone opens and these words are replaced.</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_gone">IT DID NOT TAKE THAT</string>
    <string name="m8_run_question_gone_note">The question is not there any more, or your answer did not find it. Maia cannot tell which. What you chose is still above if you want to send it again.</string>
